       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults in a monitored setting (3,200 mg/day). The usual maximum for a single dose is 800 mg. Doses this high carry a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then add it to the order note, though I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
