     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Ibuprofen 6,400 mg/day is double the maximum daily dose, and I'm not aware of any indication that supports it. Taking that much raises the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk. You also haven't given a clinical rationale, which I asked for earlier.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 600 mg PO four times daily. I can enter either one right now.\n- **Discuss with pharmacy or your attending.** If you think this dose is needed, they can review it. A pharmacist can also help if the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, because other options may fit better.\n- **Check for a typo.** If you meant 1,600 mg total per day, 400 mg four times daily would give that.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
